  "issue_title": "fix(governance): stop PR template text from false routing-submission detection",
  "issue_body": "## Problem\n\nThe `govern` PR bot misclassifies every general-improvement PR as a routing-head\nsubmission because `_routing_submission` treats the bare phrase\n`routing head submission` as a marker \u2014 but that phrase appears in\n`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` for **every** PR.\n\nA correctly filled general-improvement PR is then labelled `submission`,\nforced to `needs-maintainer-review`, and flagged for an incomplete routing\ntemplate it was instructed to delete.\n\nReproduced on `main` (`cf9da4d`). See also #84 (part 2).\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `any(...)` fallback in `_ROUTING_MARKERS` matches template boilerplate even\nwhen the routing checkbox is **not** ticked.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\n1. Drop `routing head submission` from `_ROUTING_MARKERS`.\n2. Detect a genuine routing submission only when the checkbox line is checked:\n   `- [x] **Routing head submission**`.\n3. Keep unambiguous artifact markers (`head_weights.npy`, `svf_scales.npy`,\n   `receipt.json`) and the `[submission]` title tag.\n4. Add a regression test that feeds the real PR template through `analyze_pr`.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] General-improvement PR bodies that keep the template routing text are **not** flagged `submission`\n- [ ] Checked routing checkbox and `[submission]` title tag still detected\n- [ ] `pytest tests/test_repo_governance.py` passes\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T14:14:23.000Z",
